Existing Architecture

I have a dedicated configuration repository.

Each microservice has its own configuration file (application.properties or application.yaml).

Whenever a configuration file changes, a GitHub Actions workflow is triggered automatically.

The workflow can also be executed manually using workflow_dispatch.

Each microservice currently has separate GitHub Actions workflow files for the following environments:

- DEV
- SIT
- UAT
- PROD

The pipeline currently performs these steps:

1. Checkout configuration repository.
2. Read the configuration file.
3. Create or update an OpenShift Secret called application-profile.
4. Mount the secret into the application pod.
5. Restart the deployment so the application picks up the new configuration.

This deployment flow already works perfectly.

I do NOT want to redesign or remove any existing functionality.

I only want to ADD a secure Vault integration before the OpenShift Secret is created.

